<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Catraeth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 600</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Catraeth was fought around 600 between a war band of the British kingdom of Gododdin and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a> of Deira and Bernicia. Known from the poem Y Gododdin attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aneirin">Aneirin</a>, it ended in the near-total destruction of the British warriors. Catraeth is usually identified with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catterick">Catterick</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-yorkshire">North Yorkshire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-catraeth.jpg" alt="Battle of Catraeth" width="320" height="135" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tipcake · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JacksonGododdinCoverRecreation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
